        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0128" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1917-72PubDipv06/pg91"/>

                <head>28. Circular Airgram From the United States Information Agency to All
                    Principal USIS Posts<anchor n="1" xml:id="d28-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">CA–2934</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1961-05-05">May 5, 1961</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is a need to focus USIA worldwide output more sharply in support of United
                    States policy objectives. This requires emphasis on a few priority themes and
                    subjects. It means concentrating Media output on those subjects which will be
                    most helpful to field posts in conveying these themes.</p>
                <p>The central responsibility for policy control and coordination of media content
                    is with IOP. The Agency has established the position of <pb facs="0129" n="92"
                        xml:id="pg92"/> Director of Media Content and has appointed a senior field
                        officer<anchor n="2" xml:id="d28-f2"/> to fill it. The Director of Media
                    Content reports directly to the Deputy Director of Policy and Plans.</p>
                <p>Working with the Area offices, IOP is preparing lists of priority themes and
                        subjects<anchor n="3" xml:id="d28-f3"/> for approval by the Director of
                    USIA. Working with the Media, the Director of Media Content will make certain
                    that their activities are concentrated and coordinated on these themes and
                    subjects. Working with the Area offices, he will review Media programs in terms
                    of their suitability for field needs as well as their conformity with national
                    policy and Agency priorities.</p>
                <p>The Media will continue to give special attention to meeting field requests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_MER_1">Murrow</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
